Reading the scroll *does* fire up a mailer - the one specified in 
include/unixconf.h (/usr/ucb/Mail for BSD & Ultrix or /usr/bin/mail for
SYSV and others).  However, it invokes it in the controlling tty, which
can be a pain if you're playing the X version cos' execution then
transfers  to the mail reader program in that tty.  That is, your game
stops and you have to go and find the original tty that you fired up
nethack from.

